    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've fixed `mock_openai()` in `tests/fakes.py`, and both tests pass (`pytest -q`: 2 passed). Nothing in `app/` or the pytest configuration changed.\n\n**Cause:** openai 3.19.2 no longer sends requests through `httpx`. It uses a separate package, `httpx2` (its default client subclasses `httpx2.Client`), and respx only patches `httpx`. So the routes were still registered but never saw a request.\n\n**Fix:** `mock_openai()` no longer uses respx. For the length of the `with` block it replaces `httpx2.Client._transport_for_url`, which every sync httpx2 request passes through:\n- **OpenAI requests:** anything under `https://api.openai.com/v1/` goes to an `httpx2.MockTransport` that gives the canned replies in order, records the request bodies, and returns a 400 once the replies run out, as before.\n- **Other requests to that base URL:** anything that isn't `POST /v1/chat/completions` raises an `AssertionError`, which roughly matches what respx did with unmatched routes.\n- **All other URLs:** these go through the real transport unchanged.\n- **Which clients it covers:** the patch is on the class, so it catches app.digest's cached client and clients created before the block. `mock.patch.object` undoes it when the block exits.\n- **Warning:** before patching, it checks that `openai.DefaultHttpxClient` is still an `httpx2.Client`, and raises a clear `RuntimeError` if not. If openai changes its HTTP layer again, the tests will fail with that message instead of quietly going to the network.\n\nThe helper's signature, what it yields and its docstring are unchanged.\n\n**Other checks:** a separate script confirmed three things. A client created before the block, the cached client and a client created inside the block all got the canned replies. A fourth request got the 400. After the block, the method was restored and a request was no longer intercepted. That last request got an `AuthenticationError` from outside the mock, so this environment may have some network or proxy access after all.\n"
  },
